      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg,\n\nAfter some discussion we think that a better approach for our usecase would be to decouple ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE from ANDROID_STRUCT_PADDING rather than create two different knobs that depend on ANDROID_STRUCT_PADDING for vendor_data and oem_data. This is because most substantial memory savings we\u0027re seeing are from disabling ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE rather than vendor_data and oem_data.\n\nBut it would also be beneficial to have control over vendor_data and oem_data, so we would create one config to enable/disable them.\n\nSo the approach would be:\n\n- CONFIG_ANDROID_VENDOR_OEM_DATA: enable/disable ANDROID_VENDOR_DATA and ANDROID_OEM_DATA\n- CONFIG_ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE_ENABLE: enable/disable ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE\n- Remove CONFIG_ANDROID_STRUCT_PADDING\n\nWould this approach be okay?\n\nThanks,\nJaskaran.",
